Looking at this problem:

**GCD(A!, B!)** - Since one factorial divides the other (the smaller factorial divides the larger one), GCD(A!, B!) = min(A!, B!) = min(A, B)!

The buggy code tries to compute factorials and then find GCD by brute force iteration, but:
1. A and B can be up to 10^9, so factorials would overflow
2. Even with min(A,B) ≤ 12, the brute force GCD loop iterates over the factorial value which can be up to 12! = 479001600 - this causes TLE or issues
