**Understanding:** GCD(A!, B!) = min(A, B)! because if A ≤ B, then A! divides B!, so GCD(A!, B!) = A!.

**Diagnosing the bug:**
1. The bug uses `%I64d` which is Windows/MSVC specific format specifier. On Linux (GNU C11), it should be `%lld`.
2. More critically, A and B can be up to 10^9, but min(A,B) ≤ 12. Computing factorial of up to 10^9 would overflow any integer type and cause a runtime error / TLE.
